WEBVTT

00:00:00.911 --> 00:00:09.402
An embed puts your agent on another website, for visitors who are not signed in. Here is how one is made, and what a visitor can and cannot do.

00:00:09.904 --> 00:00:20.635
In the web app, open Embeds and make a new one. Give it a name, a title and a welcome message. The preview on the right is the real widget, and it follows every change you make.

00:00:21.138 --> 00:00:32.487
Tick only the tools a visitor may use. Everything unticked is off. Then list the websites that may show the chat. A wildcard is refused, and at least one website is required.

00:00:32.988 --> 00:00:41.585
Save it, and the page gives you the snippet to paste: plain HTML, an iframe, a web component, or curl. Copy puts it on your clipboard.

00:00:42.086 --> 00:00:50.427
On the docs site, the chat bubble appears. A visitor asks a question, and the answer streams in, using only the tool the embed lists.

00:00:50.928 --> 00:01:02.213
Back in the web app, the counters show what happened, as real numbers. Rotate the key to end every open session. Disable the embed, and visitors are answered as if it never existed.

00:01:02.715 --> 00:01:08.859
That is an anonymous docs agent. The tool list, the limits and the allowed websites are what protect it.
